{
  "where_we_lag": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Etelä-Pohjanmaa lags the national average in its crude symptomatic treatment share at 28.1% (95% CI 24.5–32.1; n=152/540), whose 95% confidence interval excludes the national 39.5% (5871/14873).",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:symptomatic:Etelä_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:symptomatic"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Across overlapping treatment categories, the county's crude curative share is 30.6% (95% CI 26.8–34.6; n=165/540), whose 95% confidence interval includes the national 27.0% (4009/14873), while its crude life-prolonging share of 40.4% (95% CI 36.3–44.6; n=218/540) has a 95% confidence interval excluding the national 30.4% (4522/14873).",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:curative:Etelä_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:curative",
          "cty:life_prolonging:Etelä_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:life_prolonging"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The crude share with no treatment record within 12 months is 25.7% (95% CI 22.2–29.6; n=139/540), whose 95% confidence interval includes the national 27.5% (4089/14873), and the crude share with a recorded MDT meeting is 32.4% (95% CI 28.6–36.5; n=175/540), whose 95% confidence interval excludes the national 6.0% (893/14873).",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Etelä_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Etelä_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Public data do not measure county waiting times from symptoms, primary care, or referral to treatment start, while preliminary, unpublished national figures average 155 days from symptoms to treatment in Finland versus 107 days in Sweden and 67 days in Denmark, including 56 days for patient delay, 41 days in primary care, and 58 days in specialist care.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Symptoms",
          "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
          "bs:coverage:Referral",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start",
          "mot:total_fi",
          "mot:total_se",
          "mot:total_dk",
          "mot:patient",
          "mot:primary",
          "mot:specialist"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "how_sure_are_we": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "County treatment shares are crude figures unadjusted for age or stage, and public registry data omit referral dates, treatment start dates, and outpatient primary care visits.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:curative:Etelä_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
        "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
        "bs:coverage:Referral",
        "bs:coverage:Treatment_start",
        "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Because the crude 25.7% (95% CI 22.2–29.6; n=139/540) share with no treatment record within 12 months—which mixes untreated patients and unrecorded care—has a 95% confidence interval including the national 27.5% (4089/14873), we infer treatment recording is relatively complete, making the crude 28.1% (95% CI 24.5–32.1; n=152/540) symptomatic share against 39.5% (5871/14873) nationally unlikely to be only a recording artefact.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Etelä_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start",
          "cty:symptomatic:Etelä_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:symptomatic"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "While Kuva 16 gives digitised national age-adjusted curative reference lines of 26.7% for men and 26.9% for women (±0.5 percentage points), county shares cannot be stage-adjusted because stage is often missing; furthermore, a journal article finding about 90% HILMO diagnosis concordance covers diagnoses only, and MDT codes measure direct-contact recording rather than care.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "k16:curative:men:national",
          "k16:curative:women:national",
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:7885b0974f",
          "lit:hilmo_90",
          "bs:coverage:MDT",
          "q:39e6ba43a9"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Outpatient primary care visits are not included in the report's data and occupational health is not mentioned, imaging appears only indirectly as the basis of diagnosis in approximately 20% of cases without wait times, and HILMO records a specialist visit within 12 months for 93.6% of patients nationally without county figures or timestamps.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
          "q:323de0d90d",
          "bs:coverage:Imaging",
          "q:5eb155decc",
          "bs:coverage:First_specialist_visit"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "what_to_do_first": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "The team recommends reporting access times using THL guidance 21/2016 with handover alerts, standardising referrals and diagnostic contacts, and publishing county recording completeness for stage, drugs, and MDT.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "rec:1",
        "rec:2",
        "rec:3",
        "thl:21_2016"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "The team recommends reporting access times from referral to treatment start using THL guidance 21/2016 definitions for 16 cancers and flagging stalled handovers, since the Health Care Act sets no maximum time for a cancer suspicion and national pathways with target access times are only planned for 2026–2028, alongside a Filha diagnostics recommendation due before the 2030 interim evaluation.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:1",
          "thl:21_2016",
          "law:no_max",
          "q:4e702a20fe",
          "q:def306014c",
          "q:b326e35410",
          "q:8f358a9de6",
          "q:614febebf2",
          "q:432c0e51d6"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The team recommends a standard referral template, a primary care rule to refer persistent symptoms after a normal X-ray to a pulmonologist, and a named diagnostic-phase contact, given mentor insight that weak referrals receive lower specialist urgency ratings and that national referral criteria and care-coordinator guidance are only planned for 2026–2028, with county coordinator adoption planned for 2029–2031.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:2",
          "mentor:kaisa_referral",
          "q:556431a0c2",
          "q:37bb4c3b38",
          "q:9a1cd194f5",
          "q:c61439b30f",
          "q:fc81032a80",
          "q:e31448e9c9",
          "q:abcbb06ae3",
          "q:050ee09ebe"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "To clarify whether Etelä-Pohjanmaa's crude 28.1% (95% CI 24.5–32.1; n=152/540) symptomatic share versus 39.5% (5871/14873) nationally and crude 32.4% (95% CI 28.6–36.5; n=175/540) MDT share versus 6.0% (893/14873) reflect care or coding, the team recommends publishing county recording completeness for stage, drug treatment, and MDT coding while a national quality registry targeting 90% coverage is planned.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:3",
          "cty:symptomatic:Etelä_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:symptomatic",
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Etelä_Pohjanmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "q:7885b0974f",
          "q:950a2f797b",
          "q:4c7a01d84c",
          "q:f07a34a300",
          "q:4a856bd695"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
